        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Roles: Governor of Sheerness Fort and the Isle of Sheppey\n- Places: Sheerness, Isle of Sheppey, Medway estuary\n- People: Stapleton Cotton, 1st Viscount Combermere\n- Roles: British Army officer, diplomat, politician\n\nFacts:\n- The Governor of Sheerness Fort and the Isle of Sheppey was a military officer who commanded the fortifications at Sheerness on the Isle of Sheppey.\n- Sheerness and the Isle of Sheppey formed part of the defences of the Medway estuary.\n- Stapleton Cotton, 1st Viscount Combermere, was born on 14 November 1773.\n- Stapleton Cotton, 1st Viscount Combermere, was a British Army officer, diplomat, and politician.\n- Stapleton Cotton, 1st Viscount Combermere, died on 21 February 1865.",
